      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] Setting `image-data-offset-bytes \u003d \u003c400\u003e` here while keeping `frame-size \u003d \u003c25600\u003e` creates an impossible configuration for the driver.\n\nFor `FINGERPRINT_CAPTURE_TYPE_SIMPLE_IMAGE`, the driver now calculates `offset \u003d 400` and `frame_size \u003d 25600`. It then checks if `offset + frame_size \u003e image_buf_size`. If the caller provides a buffer of `frame_size` (25600), the check will fail: `400 + 25600 (26000) \u003e 25600` is true, so the driver will return `-EINVAL`.\n\nIf this mode is not supposed to have an offset, this value should be 0. If it IS supposed to have an offset, `frame-size` must be increased to at least 26000 to accommodate both the offset and the pixel data.",
